                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbd9d2bd-7e1e-490b-967c-dfcbab14239b",
                                                "sense_id": "6367e1ee-0162-3beb-9c88-1e4166654690",
                                                "text": "Observations on sea-anemones in dimly lighted situations, such as under bridges and so forth, showed that these animals were more or less continuously expanded, but aside from such exceptions it was clear that Metridium in its natural surroundings exhibited a well-marked nychthemeral rhythm."
                                            }
